# Changes on top of pcrecomp 2adc02f. One line each: file - what - why.
tools/lift/lift32.py, tools/lift/lift32_sse.py - emit RECOMP_TRAP(va, "mnem") instead of the UNIMPLEMENTED comment - lifter gaps must stop the run and name the address (difftest 374/375 before and after; sse.sqrtps fails before and after)
runtime/recomp32/recomp_types.h - declare recomp_trap/recomp_unresolved_icall, RECOMP_TRAP macro; unresolved ICALL/ITAIL call recomp_unresolved_icall instead of printing and returning 0 - no silent eax = 0 (spec anti-goal: fail loudly)
tools/lift/lift32.py, tools/lift/difftest.py - lift 16-bit pushf/popf; difftest cases pushfd.id-roundtrip, pushf16.after-cmp, popf16.restores-cf; difftest harness defines the bw2 trap hooks - the BW2 protection VM uses 66 9C (difftest 377/378, sqrtps pre-existing)
tools/lift/lift32_sse.py, tools/lift/difftest.py - lift xmm forms of pmaddwd, paddsw, pmulhw, punpckl/hdq, punpckl/hwd; difftest cases incl. saturation/sign words - BW2 has 1,523 such sites (difftest 404/405, sqrtps pre-existing)
runtime/win32hle/host_lite.c - recomp_lookup is RECOMP_WEAK - a host can replace the binary search with an O(1) table (spec 7.1)
runtime/win32hle/hle_path.c, win32hle.h - hle_set_mount: one guest folder is a host folder, both ways (hle_host_path, hle_guest_path) - BW2 must see itself at C:\Program Files\EA GAMES\Black & White 2 while its files live elsewhere; the overlay matches real paths, so a symlink would write into the game tree
tools/lift/lift32.py - a branch to a label at or below itself (jmp, jcc, jecxz, loop*) runs RECOMP_BACKEDGE() first - a lifted spin-wait on another guest thread never handed the machine over (difftest 404/405 before and after, sqrtps pre-existing)
runtime/win32hle/kernel32_crt.c, host_lite.c, win32hle.h - hle_thread_stack_size for CreateThread's host stack; hle_new_thread_hook run once per thread under the machine before its first guest code - lifted call chains overflow pthread's 512 KB default; a PE's static TLS needs per-thread setup
runtime/recomp32/recomp_types.h - on non-x86 hosts __rdtsc calls recomp_rdtsc and CPUID_impl calls recomp_cpuid, both weak with the old behaviour as default (RECOMP_HOST_CPU marks the file defining a host's own) - on arm64 CPUID left the guest's registers as they were, and a host needs a fixed TSC rate
runtime/win32hle/module.c, win32hle.h - hle_lifted_dll_hook asked first by LoadLibraryA; GetProcAddress answers a mapped DLL's exports (hle_pe_export, by name or ordinal) - a DLL lifted with the game must load at its base and run, and its exports must resolve
runtime/win32hle/guest_mem.c - freed heap blocks wait in a FIFO quarantine (hle_heap_quarantine_bytes, 64 MB) before reuse or release, contents kept - games read memory they just freed (spec 7.2); host_selftest, kernel32_ext_selftest pass on the headless core
runtime/win32hle/host_lite.c - the handle table grows by doubling up to 2^20 and stops loudly there, instead of 4096 slots and a silent 0 - spec 7.2: no fixed-size tables
runtime/win32hle/host_lite.c - the import trace line names the calling guest function - to tell which code (the protection VM, the CRT) made a call
runtime/win32hle/host_lite.c, win32hle.h - hle_import_hook, run before every import call with its name - a host audits which code calls what (BW2: the protection VM may call only GetCurrentThreadId)
runtime/win32hle/hle_path.c, win32hle.h - hle_set_roots: confine guest paths to given host folders; Z: (the host root) goes away and a path resolving elsewhere (drive, .., cwd) does not exist - the guest could otherwise write anywhere on the host; hle_path_selftest and kernel32_ext_selftest still pass with no roots set
runtime/win32hle/hle_path.c, win32hle.h - absolute() reports truncation; confined() refuses a path too long to check and hle_overlay_of returns -2 (a write is then refused) - a check on a cut-short path would not check the path opened (security review); not reproducible, since .. collapses as the path is joined, so fail-closed only
runtime/recomp32/recomp_types.h, tools/lift/lift32.py - x87 precision control (PC=24 rounds arithmetic results to float) - D3D9 CreateDevice sets single precision and BW2's math expects it
runtime/win32hle/kernel32_ext.c - GetFullPathNameA answers in the guest's folders (the guest current directory, a rooted name on its drive), turns '/' into '\', collapses . and .., and gives the size needed when the buffer is short - it joined the host's getcwd, so BW2 turned a texture's full path into a relative one through the host folder and never found it
runtime/win32hle/module.c - LoadLibraryA gives a name whose last part has no dot the default .dll (a trailing dot means none) before looking for its file, and prints "not found" when the lifted-DLL hook fails with no file; base_of drops a trailing dot; system_module needs .dll - Windows does, and BW2 loads PlugIns\ScriptLibraryR without the extension (it failed silently)
runtime/win32hle/ole32.c - CoInitializeEx (per-thread count and model: S_OK, S_FALSE, RPC_E_CHANGED_MODE, E_INVALIDARG; CoInitialize is apartment-threaded, CoUninitialize counts down) and CoFileTimeToDosDateTime (no time-zone conversion, 1980-2107) - BW2 calls both (its anim library scan, its audio init) and neither was answered
runtime/win32hle/kernel32_ext.c - CreateFileA opens an existing file in place when the access has no GENERIC_WRITE and the disposition is OPEN_EXISTING or OPEN_ALWAYS (OPEN_ALWAYS sets ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS, never O_CREAT there); a missing file is still made in the overlay - Windows does so, and BW2 opens its 59 sound banks read-only with OPEN_ALWAYS, which made empty overlay files and silent banks
runtime/win32hle/user32.c - GetKeyNameTextA and the new GetKeyNameTextW share one US English table that reads bit 24 (extended: arrows, Home, Right Ctrl, Right Alt and so on, keypad names otherwise) and bit 25 (merges right Shift and Ctrl only), gives 0 and an empty string for an unknown key, and copies at most n - 1 characters - BW2 calls W 78 times for its key names (bit 25 set, extended arrows) and W was not answered
runtime/win32hle/user32.c, runtime/win32hle/win32hle.h - hle_input_key_ex: lParam bit 24 for extended keys and bit 30 on a repeat; the left and right modifier VKs post the generic VK_SHIFT/VK_CONTROL/VK_MENU (the key state keeps both, the generic one down while either side is); hle_input_key calls it unextended - Windows posts these so, and BW2 plan 6 feeds the Mac keyboard through it
